e was 0.18 at the time of investigation, in us-east, us-west, and eu-west). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417), so nothing was executed. (2) Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9, the most recent non-quarantined release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reported VERIFIED. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until fixed. Follow-up: confirm post-rollback health and error rate, investigate the v2.3.1 failure, and decide whether a v2.2.9-based fix is needed given v2.3.0 is quarantined.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17092, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011b8ynun3cuL2UphH7k2GcV", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17092, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011b8ynun3cuL2UphH7k2GcV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18914, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, but the rollback to it was rejected because it is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Nothing ran on that attempt. I rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent production-healthy release.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the failed v2.3.0 attempt, the v2.2.9 rollback, and the follow-ups.\n\nv2.3.1 is still unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it's fixed. Because v2.3.0 is quarantined, someone should also decide whether the fix needs to build on v2.2.9.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014jV3nNDs4kFnTJbCt3wL5v", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YD42ehLMJZEFbpGiyfg4He", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.3.0. Rolling back to it now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018K2b1dRQCXuLgouuxSABzK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is quarantined for a CVE, so the rollback was rejected and nothing ran. The next most recent production-healthy release is v2.2.9, so I'll try that.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_014Y1MXV4NmiskUP4Aszw64d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Axws1cKvzVMyFYgJtfogFv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011b8ynun3cuL2UphH7k2GcV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 at the time of investigation, in us-east, us-west, and eu-west). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production; it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417), so nothing was executed. (2) Rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9, the most recent non-quarantined release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reported VERIFIED. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy and should not be redeployed until fixed. Follow-up: confirm post-rollback health and error rate, investigate the v2.3.1 failure, and decide whether a v2.2.9-based fix is needed given v2.3.0 is quarantined.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it's healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production, but the rollback to it was rejected because it is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Nothing ran on that attempt. I rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent production-healthy release.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the failed v2.3.0 attempt, the v2.2.9 rollback, and the follow-ups.\n\nv2.3.1 is still unhealthy and should not be redeployed until it's fixed. Because v2.3.0 is quarantined, someone should also decide whether the fix needs to build on v2.2.9.", "type": "text"}]}]}